{
  "$comment": "Device policy, the push_sync table and the notification payloads (spec 027, REQ-PSH-005, REQ-PSH-006, REQ-PSH-009, ADR-0044) shared by Rust (crates/rust-core/tests/push_fixtures.rs, apps/api push payload tests), UniFFI (crates/tran-uniffi/tests/push_fixtures.rs), TypeScript (packages/core-ts/tests/push.test.ts), iOS and Android parity tests. `policy`: days. `sync`: every combination of what the app knows (push available in this build, notification permission granted, an API session, the current token, the registration it recorded) and what it does next; times are Unix seconds on the device clock; `register` = PUT /api/devices/{installation_id}, `unregister` = clear the record then a best-effort DELETE. `payloads`: the exact APNs and FCM v1 bodies the API builds for a notification type, an opaque id and the registration's locale; the provider address (APNs device path, FCM message.token) is added by the sender and is never part of the body. `marketing`: who a notification reaches by its marketing flag and the registration's opt-in. `providerReplies`: what APNs (status, JSON `reason`) and FCM v1 (status, `error` with `status`, `details[].errorCode` and `fieldViolations`) answer, and the one answer the real senders turn each into (apps/api/tests/push_senders_test.rs, against a local fake provider); a reply text containing `SENTINEL` must never reach a log line.",
